# ── Chapter 6 fidelity pins: "Who Owes, and What Follows" ──────────────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/06-who-owes-and-what-follows.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # the real check — the line above cannot see
#                        # the cross-file reconciliation or the prose guards
#
# The chapter's case lists the child fixture and eight obligations fixtures —
# the five forms of public responsibility, delegation without discharge, and
# the refusal to read a private duty out of subject matter alone:
#   tests/pins/records/child_with_nobody/fixture.nibli
#   tests/pins/obligations/case-001 .. case-008
# It also supplies tests/pins/scarcity/worked/competing-claims/fixture.nibli
# for the preceding chapter's waiting claimant and separate allocation duties.
#
# The rest of the chapter's chain rests on the families' own sequences, which
# this file cites rather than duplicates:
#   tests/pins/obligations/                     FS-CCE-198..222, the typed
#                                               three-place duty and its bridge
#   tests/pins/justice/appeal/request-without-operator-or-previous-permission
#   tests/pins/justice/nonresponse/positive      and its silence-only control
#   tests/pins/justice/defect/wrong-version-cannot-withdraw-real-relief
#   tests/pins/public-safety/                    the protective-power route
#   tests/pins/ecology/ecological-record-defect  and the animal remedy orders
#   tests/pins/scarcity/nonresponse/positive
# Each derives its family's duty on a named reader or executor. None of them
# establishes that a reader received anything or that anybody acted.
#
# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE: a FALSE is pinned only where the KB could have said
# TRUE, and the comment says what would flip it.

:expect-pins 75

# ── "Public responsibility around it takes distinct forms." ────────────────
# Respect, protection, fulfilment, continuity, remedy — one typed duty each.
? obliged(OblPositive198Bearer, OblPositive198Duty, OblPositive198Standard).
# => TRUE

? obliged(OblPositive199Bearer, OblPositive199Duty, OblPositive199Standard).
# => TRUE

? obliged(OblPositive200Bearer, OblPositive200Duty, OblPositive200Standard).
# => TRUE

? obliged(OblPositive201Bearer, OblPositive201Duty, OblPositive201Standard).
# => TRUE

? obliged(OblPositive202Bearer, OblPositive202Duty, OblPositive202Standard).
# => TRUE

# ── "A public function cannot shed its duties by being contracted out" ─────
# The performer carries the duty for that work, and the public duty stays where
# it was: both conclusions, not one replacing the other.
? obliged(OblPositive203Bearer, OblPositive203Duty, OblPositive203Standard).
# => TRUE

? obliged(State, OblPositive203Duty, OblPositive203Standard).
# => TRUE

# ── "A private duty must be stated expressly for the function undertaken" ──
? obliged(OblPositive204Bearer, OblPositive204Duty, OblPositive204Standard).
# => TRUE

# "The reverse boundary matters just as much." Subject matter alone concludes
# no private duty; what would flip this is an express duty record for the
# function, which case-007 above supplies for its own bearer.
? prevents(OblPositive205Bearer, SubjectMatterOnlyPrivateDutyInference).
# => TRUE

# ── "Missing papers cannot suspend urgent human protection or animal care." ─
# A direct urgent-care request with no owner, taxon or official record. It
# creates a duty, not personhood and not proof that a rescue occurred.
challenge(ECReaderHelper, ECReaderAnimal, ECReaderUrgentRequest).
observe(ECReaderHelper, ECReaderUrgentRequest, ECUrgentPlausibleAnimalProtectionRequest, ECRequestKindScope).
? obliged(State, ECProvidePromptSafeAnimalProtectionAndNecessaryCareBeforeRecordReconciliation, ECReaderUrgentRequest).
# => TRUE

? person(ECReaderAnimal).
# => FALSE

# ── "a duty here is a statement that somebody must answer" ─────────────────
# The typed duty is a conclusion, never a verdict somebody writes.
:refuse reasoning /declared derived-only/
obliged(OblPositive198Bearer, OblPositive198Duty, ForgedObligationStandard).

# ── The child with nobody ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "no household, relationship, association or charity is presumed to provide
# another person's floor, so the absence of all of them subtracts nothing"
? prevents(Nell, KinshipNoPersonalCareDebt).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, PublicFirstCareContinuity).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Dwell, Nell).
# => TRUE

# "Nothing between the birth entry and the debt asks who is caring for the
# child." The record holds no family entry for Nell and the debt is unmoved.
? family(Nell).
# => FALSE

# ── The one duty that does not wait to be asked ──────────────────────────────
# Article 1c's whole body is `person($x)`, so it holds for the record of one
# line and holds identically for everybody else. There is nothing in it a
# person could fail and nothing about it a record could withhold.
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Nell).
# => TRUE

# The escalation waits for an entry, and the entry takes no seat, no
# relationship and no standing.
? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Nell).
# => FALSE

observe(Bystander, NellAlone, Nell, UninitiatedAssistanceScope).

? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Nell).
# => TRUE

# "the entry concludes nothing about the person it names"
? prisoner(Nell).
# => FALSE

? false(Nell).
# => FALSE

? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE

# "The same entry records an encounter, so it also gives standing to the person
# it names, even someone this report alone has entered, and the review duty
# reaches them too."
? person(BystanderSawSomeone).
# => FALSE

observe(Bystander, SomeoneAlone, BystanderSawSomeone, UninitiatedAssistanceScope).
? person(BystanderSawSomeone).
# => TRUE

? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, BystanderSawSomeone).
# => TRUE

# "A duty is not an arrival" — nothing reads either duty, and no actuality moves.
? eats(Nell).
# => FALSE

# The waiting claim retains a responsible manager and an independent reader.
# The stateful challenge and qualified comparison-defect sequence is
# tests/pins/scarcity/worked/challenge-and-comparison-defect/expect.pins.nibli.
? obliged(ScarcityWorkedManager, PublishComparativeAllocationReasonsAndRejectedAlternatives, ScarcityWorkedRecord).
# => TRUE
? obliged(ScarcityWorkedManager, RepairAndReassessTheRecordedShortfall, ScarcityWaitingShortfallRecord).
# => TRUE
? obliged(ScarcityWaitingShortfallReader, VerifyTheShortfallWasRecordedAsFailure, ScarcityWaitingShortfallRecord).
# => TRUE
? complete(ScarcityWaitingShortfallRecord, ReviewedScarcityShortfall, IndivisibleEssentialPowerUnit).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Healthy, ScarcityWaitingClaimant).
# => TRUE
? healthy(ScarcityWaitingClaimant).
# => FALSE

# ── When failure is general (revision item 38) ─────────────────────────────
# "A pattern arrives as an independently certified finding about a publicly
#  answerable tier, never a count and never a finding about a person." Fresh
#  constants, so no cast verdict moves.
public(NorthProvision).
authorized(PatternSource, FloorShortfallPatternSourceAuthority, Pattern_North).
authorized(PatternReviewer, IndependentFloorShortfallPatternReviewAuthority, Pattern_North).
observe(PatternSource, Pattern_North, NorthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
observe(PatternReviewer, Pattern_North, NorthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, DecideWhetherTheCertifiedFloorShortfallIsAnUnconstitutionalStateOfAffairs, Pattern_North).
# => TRUE

# Certification alone obliges no plan: the Constitutional Court decides first.
? obliged(FSBOD_02, AdoptAPublicPlanWithReasonsDeadlinesAndASourceBoundEnd, Pattern_North).
# => FALSE

# "Its declaration obliges the Assembly to adopt a public plan with reasons,
#  deadlines and a source-bound end, the failing tier to carry it out, and the
#  audit body to monitor it and publish the follow-up."
authorized(FSBOD_18, UnconstitutionalStateOfAffairsDeclarationAuthority, Pattern_North).
observe(FSBOD_18, Pattern_North, NorthProvision, UnconstitutionalFloorShortfallDeclarationScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_02, AdoptAPublicPlanWithReasonsDeadlinesAndASourceBoundEnd, Pattern_North).
# => TRUE
? obliged(NorthProvision, CarryOutThePublicPlanForTheCertifiedShortfall, Pattern_North).
# => TRUE
? obliged(FSBOD_19, MonitorThePlanAndPublishTheFollowUp, Pattern_North).
# => TRUE
? obliged(FSBOD_18, OrderInterimMeasuresSecuringTheMinimumWithoutAdministeringTheService, Pattern_North).
# => FALSE

# "If the monitor and a separate reviewer certify that the Assembly has not
#  adopted a plan, the Court owes interim measures that secure the minimum
#  without administering the service, and the treasury owes the minimum the
#  first claim on funds."
authorized(FSBOD_19, FloorPlanNonresponseSourceAuthority, Pattern_North).
authorized(PlanReviewer, IndependentFloorPlanNonresponseReviewAuthority, Pattern_North).
observe(FSBOD_19, Pattern_North, FSBOD_02, FloorPlanNonresponseScope).
observe(PlanReviewer, Pattern_North, FSBOD_02, FloorPlanNonresponseScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, OrderInterimMeasuresSecuringTheMinimumWithoutAdministeringTheService, Pattern_North).
# => TRUE
? obliged(FSBOD_07, GiveTheFloorMinimumTheFirstClaimOnFunds, Pattern_North).
# => TRUE

# A tier cannot certify its own pattern.
public(SouthProvision).
authorized(SouthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternSourceAuthority, Pattern_South).
authorized(PatternReviewer, IndependentFloorShortfallPatternReviewAuthority, Pattern_South).
observe(SouthProvision, Pattern_South, SouthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
observe(PatternReviewer, Pattern_South, SouthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, DecideWhetherTheCertifiedFloorShortfallIsAnUnconstitutionalStateOfAffairs, Pattern_South).
# => FALSE

# One attester alone certifies nothing.
authorized(PatternSource, FloorShortfallPatternSourceAuthority, Pattern_Lone).
observe(PatternSource, Pattern_Lone, NorthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, DecideWhetherTheCertifiedFloorShortfallIsAnUnconstitutionalStateOfAffairs, Pattern_Lone).
# => FALSE

# The reviewer must certify the tier the source names. A split certification,
# even with a declaration beside it, obliges no decision and no plan.
authorized(PatternSource, FloorShortfallPatternSourceAuthority, Pattern_Split).
authorized(PatternReviewer, IndependentFloorShortfallPatternReviewAuthority, Pattern_Split).
observe(PatternSource, Pattern_Split, NorthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
observe(PatternReviewer, Pattern_Split, SouthProvision, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
authorized(FSBOD_18, UnconstitutionalStateOfAffairsDeclarationAuthority, Pattern_Split).
observe(FSBOD_18, Pattern_Split, NorthProvision, UnconstitutionalFloorShortfallDeclarationScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, DecideWhetherTheCertifiedFloorShortfallIsAnUnconstitutionalStateOfAffairs, Pattern_Split).
# => FALSE
? obliged(FSBOD_02, AdoptAPublicPlanWithReasonsDeadlinesAndASourceBoundEnd, Pattern_Split).
# => FALSE

# A declaration without a certified pattern obliges no plan.
authorized(FSBOD_18, UnconstitutionalStateOfAffairsDeclarationAuthority, Pattern_Bare).
observe(FSBOD_18, Pattern_Bare, NorthProvision, UnconstitutionalFloorShortfallDeclarationScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_02, AdoptAPublicPlanWithReasonsDeadlinesAndASourceBoundEnd, Pattern_Bare).
# => FALSE

# "Never a finding about a person." A pattern naming someone who holds no
# public answerability certifies nothing and gives that person no duty.
authorized(PatternSource, FloorShortfallPatternSourceAuthority, Pattern_Person).
authorized(PatternReviewer, IndependentFloorShortfallPatternReviewAuthority, Pattern_Person).
observe(PatternSource, Pattern_Person, Bela, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
observe(PatternReviewer, Pattern_Person, Bela, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
authorized(FSBOD_18, UnconstitutionalStateOfAffairsDeclarationAuthority, Pattern_Person).
observe(FSBOD_18, Pattern_Person, Bela, UnconstitutionalFloorShortfallDeclarationScope).

? authority(Bela).
# => FALSE
? obliged(FSBOD_18, DecideWhetherTheCertifiedFloorShortfallIsAnUnconstitutionalStateOfAffairs, Pattern_Person).
# => FALSE
? obliged(Bela, CarryOutThePublicPlanForTheCertifiedShortfall, Pattern_Person).
# => FALSE

# A plan duty is not provision: the waiting claimant's care remains owed and
# undelivered.
? healthy(ScarcityWaitingClaimant).
# => FALSE

# ── A claim that fails, from first contact to remedy ─────────────────────────
# "A claim that fails": one person followed through every office that owes
# them something, each failing in turn. Every constant is fresh, so nothing
# here reaches the cast, and the section adds no timing or staffing.

# First contact makes Juno a person, owed the floor, the advocate's first move
# and the common tier's backstop, with nothing asked about papers or family.
at(Juno, FirstContact).

? person(Juno).
# => TRUE
? owe(State, Eats, Juno).
# => TRUE
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Juno).
# => TRUE
? obliged(CommonTier, BackstopTheFloorForEveryPersonInTheJurisdiction, Juno).
# => TRUE

# A witness authorised for Juno records where Juno is present: the region owes
# provision and the locality reach and delivery.
authorized(JunoPresenceWitness, FloorPresenceWitness, Juno).
observe(JunoPresenceWitness, Juno, JunoRegion, FloorPresenceRegionScope).
observe(JunoPresenceWitness, Juno, JunoLocality, FloorPresenceLocalityScope).

? obliged(JunoRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Juno).
# => TRUE
? obliged(JunoLocality, ReachAndDeliverTheFloorLocally, Juno).
# => TRUE

# Provision recorded only by the provider: a kitchen records serving Juno and
# witnesses its own record. No food conclusion follows; the debt stands.
receives(Juno, JunoMeal, JunoKitchen).
authorized(JunoKitchen, DeliveryWitness, Juno).
observe(JunoKitchen, JunoMeal, Juno, FoodScope).

? eats(Juno).
# => FALSE
? owe(State, Eats, Juno).
# => TRUE

# Nobody begins. Until somebody records that, the alternate owes no review; a
# passerby's entry lands the review duty, and anybody may write it.
? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Juno).
# => FALSE

observe(JunoPasserby, JunoAloneEntry, Juno, UninitiatedAssistanceScope).

? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Juno).
# => TRUE

# Neither office acts. No rule reads a duty, so their silence concludes nothing
# about Juno: no credibility finding, no custody, and both duties still owed.
? false(Juno).
# => FALSE
? prisoner(Juno).
# => FALSE
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Juno).
# => TRUE
? obliged(IndependentRightsAlternate, ReviewWhetherAssistanceWasInitiatedForThisPerson, Juno).
# => TRUE

# The region fails. An auditor and an independent reviewer, neither of them the
# region, certify the failure and name the common tier: continuity passes up,
# the region's own duty stands, and Juno is still owed food nobody has shown.
authorized(JunoAuditor, FloorFailureSourceAuthority, JunoFailure).
authorized(JunoFailureReviewer, IndependentFloorFailureReviewAuthority, JunoFailure).
observe(JunoAuditor, JunoFailure, JunoRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(JunoFailureReviewer, JunoFailure, JunoRegion, FloorFailedTierScope).
observe(JunoAuditor, JunoFailure, CommonTier, FloorContinuityTierScope).
observe(JunoFailureReviewer, JunoFailure, CommonTier, FloorContinuityTierScope).

? obliged(CommonTier, AssumeFloorContinuityForTheCertifiedFailure, JunoFailure).
# => TRUE
? obliged(JunoRegion, ProvideTheFloorWhereThePersonIsPresent, Juno).
# => TRUE
? eats(Juno).
# => FALSE

# The failure is general. A certified pattern in Juno's region reaches the
# Constitutional Court; its declaration obliges the Assembly's plan; the
# Assembly's certified nonresponse obliges interim measures and gives the
# minimum the first claim on funds.
public(JunoRegion).
authorized(JunoPatternSource, FloorShortfallPatternSourceAuthority, JunoPattern).
authorized(JunoPatternReviewer, IndependentFloorShortfallPatternReviewAuthority, JunoPattern).
observe(JunoPatternSource, JunoPattern, JunoRegion, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).
observe(JunoPatternReviewer, JunoPattern, JunoRegion, FloorShortfallPatternTierScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, DecideWhetherTheCertifiedFloorShortfallIsAnUnconstitutionalStateOfAffairs, JunoPattern).
# => TRUE

authorized(FSBOD_18, UnconstitutionalStateOfAffairsDeclarationAuthority, JunoPattern).
observe(FSBOD_18, JunoPattern, JunoRegion, UnconstitutionalFloorShortfallDeclarationScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_02, AdoptAPublicPlanWithReasonsDeadlinesAndASourceBoundEnd, JunoPattern).
# => TRUE
? obliged(JunoRegion, CarryOutThePublicPlanForTheCertifiedShortfall, JunoPattern).
# => TRUE

authorized(FSBOD_19, FloorPlanNonresponseSourceAuthority, JunoPattern).
authorized(JunoPlanReviewer, IndependentFloorPlanNonresponseReviewAuthority, JunoPattern).
observe(FSBOD_19, JunoPattern, FSBOD_02, FloorPlanNonresponseScope).
observe(JunoPlanReviewer, JunoPattern, FSBOD_02, FloorPlanNonresponseScope).

? obliged(FSBOD_18, OrderInterimMeasuresSecuringTheMinimumWithoutAdministeringTheService, JunoPattern).
# => TRUE
? obliged(FSBOD_07, GiveTheFloorMinimumTheFirstClaimOnFunds, JunoPattern).
# => TRUE

# The remedy is owed, not performed. Juno keeps standing and free movement
# throughout, and nothing yet shows that food arrived.
? person(Juno).
# => TRUE
? travel(Juno).
# => TRUE
? eats(Juno).
# => FALSE
